### PILLAR 1: Historical, Classical & High Ornamentation

#### 01. Neoclassical
* **Historical Origin:** 18th-century European revival of classical Greece and Rome.
* **Core Identifiers:** Strict bilateral symmetry, Greco-Roman architectural orders (Ionic, Corinthian), laurel wreaths, fluted columns, low-saturation marble.
* **Palette:** Carrara white, stone grey, antique gold, imperial navy, muted terracotta.
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `Neoclassical style, Greco-Roman architecture, Corinthian columns, bilateral symmetry, Didone serif typography, Carrara marble texture, gold leaf filigree, studio rim lighting, timeless editorial composition`.

#### 02. Baroque
* **Historical Origin:** 17th-century European counter-reformation art.
* **Core Identifiers:** Intense theatrical drama, explosive visual movement, rich heavy drapery, curved ornamental flourishes, extreme contrast.
* **Palette:** Deep crimson, burnt umber, royal gold, obsidian, deep bronze.
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `Baroque aesthetic, extreme chiaroscuro, dramatic Caravaggio lighting, heavy gold leaf gilding, opulent ornamental flourishes, dynamic diagonal motion, theatrical atmosphere, hyper-detailed oil painting`.

#### 03. Victorian
* **Historical Origin:** 19th-century British industrial/imperial era.
* **Core Identifiers:** Heavy ornamental complexity, damask and filigree wall patterns, engraved flourishes, dense visual framing, cast-iron motifs.
* **Palette:** Deep forest green, burgundy, deep plum, brass, tarnished gold.
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `Victorian era aesthetic, ornate wood carving, damask wallpaper pattern, engraved lithograph line work, vintage brass accents, dark moody study lighting, historical depth`.

#### 04. Gothic
* **Historical Origin:** 12th–16th century European ecclesiastical architecture & late Romanticism.
* **Core Identifiers:** Ogival (pointed) arches, ribbed vaults, stained glass illumination, blackletter typography, stone gargoyles, verticality.
* **Palette:** Jet black, charcoal slate, blood red, royal amethyst, aged cathedral stone.
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `Gothic revival style, pointed arches, stained glass rose window, blackletter calligraphy, stone texture, high contrast shadows, mist, raytraced atmospheric fog`.

#### 05. Tenebrism
* **Historical Origin:** 17th-century painting school popularized by Caravaggio.
* **Core Identifiers:** Heightened chiaroscuro where darkness dominates; spotlight effect slicing across the subject; pitch-black non-descript background.
* **Palette:** Pitch black (`#000000`), warm amber, ochre highlights, skin tones illuminated through deep shadows.
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `Tenebrism style, Caravaggesque lighting, deep opaque black backgrounds, directional spotlighting, extreme light-to-dark contrast, painterly oil texture, hyper-dramatic chiaroscuro`.

#### 06. Art Nouveau
* **Historical Origin:** Late 19th-century decorative arts reaction against academic art.
* **Core Identifiers:** Sinuous, whiplash lines, sinuous botanical structures, Alphonse Mucha-style framing, hand-drawn flowing typography, organic asymmetry.
* **Palette:** Sage green, mustard, peacock blue, dusty rose, burnt copper.
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `Art Nouveau style, Alphonse Mucha illustration, sinuous whiplash lines, organic botanical framing, flowing curvilinear forms, stained glass flat color fills, vintage lithograph texture`.

#### 07. Art Deco
* **Historical Origin:** 1920s interwar Paris & New York decorative movement.
* **Core Identifiers:** Streamlined industrial geometric shapes, chevron/sunburst patterns, stepped structural facades, metallic inlays, luxurious symmetry.
* **Palette:** High-polish chrome, black obsidian, burnished gold, deep emerald, sapphire.
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `Art Deco movement, Chrysler building geometry, stepped chevrons, sunburst motifs, polished gold and obsidian chrome, symmetrical luxury typography, 1920s Gatsby glamour`.

#### 08. Filigree & Acanthus
* **Historical Origin:** Classical architectural stonework & fine goldsmithing.
* **Core Identifiers:** Intertwined curling leaf forms (Acanthus mollis), lacework metal wires, curling tendrils, continuous relief patterns.
* **Palette:** Gilded yellow gold, antique silver, patinated bronze, muted plaster white.
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `Intricate acanthus leaf ornamentation, fine filigree wirework, curling botanical relief, metallic gold wire embroidery, micro-embossing, luxury baroque details`.

