### PILLAR 3: Retro-Futurism, Tech Revival & Digital

#### 18. Pixel Art
* **Historical Origin:** 1980s 8-bit / 16-bit arcade and console video games (NES, SNES, Genesis).
* **Core Identifiers:** Hard visible square pixel grid, manual dithering patterns, restricted color indexes (16–256 colors), strict lack of anti-aliasing.
* **Palette:** Palette swaps, EGA/CGA modes, 16-bit saturated palettes.
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `16-bit pixel art style, hand-crafted sprite aesthetics, manual dithering, retro video game screen, crisp pixel grid, authentic color banding, nostalgia gaming render`.

#### 19. Y2K Aesthetic
* **Historical Origin:** Circa 1997–2003 hardware, music videos, and fashion (the Dot-com boom era).
* **Core Identifiers:** Inflatable translucent plastics, chrome and liquid-metal gradients, rave typography, cyber-futuristic optimism, futuristic sunglasses, lens flare reflections.
* **Palette:** Icy metallic silver, bubblegum pink, iridescent cyan, translucent lime green.
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `Y2K aesthetic, 2000s cyber-optimism, liquid chrome typography, translucent iridescent plastic, glossy lens flares, 3D bubbly forms, late-90s futuristic render`.

#### 20. Neo Frutiger Aero
* **Historical Origin:** 2004–2012 tech design language (Windows 7/Vista, early OS X, skeuomorphism).
* **Core Identifiers:** Glossy wet reflections, clear blue skies, tropical fish, water droplets, vibrant green grass inside tech devices, ray of sunlight lens flares, friendly humanist sans-serifs (Frutiger, Segoe).
* **Palette:** Aqua marine, clean sky blue, brilliant grass green, gloss white.
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `Frutiger Aero aesthetic, glossy skeuomorphic surfaces, transparent water droplets, hyper-clean aqua blue tones, blooming sunshine, green ecological tech optimism, 2008 high-definition render`.

#### 21. Vaporwave
* **Historical Origin:** Early 2010s internet subculture and musical genre critiquing consumer capitalism.
* **Core Identifiers:** Greco-Roman busts (David, Venus), Windows 95/98 window dialog boxes, checkered 3D wireframe floors stretching to the horizon, glitch VHS scanlines, Japanese kanji banners.
* **Palette:** Lilac purple, pastel cyan, neon sunset magenta, soft peach.
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `Vaporwave aesthetic, classical Greek statue bust, Windows 95 desktop icons, retro 3D grid horizon, lo-fi VHS tracking errors, Japanese typography, Arizona Green Tea pastel colors`.

#### 22. Synthwave / Retrowave
* **Historical Origin:** 1980s pop culture nostalgia; Outrun aesthetic (Miami Vice, Tron, Blade Runner).
* **Core Identifiers:** Neon grid receding to an oversized wireframe sunset, vector sports cars (Ferrari Testarossa, DeLorean), neon palm tree silhouettes, 3D extruded chrome typography.
* **Palette:** Electric magenta, laser cyan, deep neon indigo, blinding chrome yellow.
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `Synthwave 80s aesthetic, neon wireframe horizon, glowing laser sunset, chrome typography, Outrun visual style, volumetric purple mist, dark retrofuturistic cyber scene`.

#### 23. Cybercore / Cybergoth
* **Historical Origin:** Early-2000s underground hacker communities, terminal aesthetics, and Industrial sci-fi.
* **Core Identifiers:** Monospaced green terminal cascades, cybernetic bio-interfaces, glitch data compression artifacts, HUD telemetry, industrial tech-wear motifs.
* **Palette:** Matrix green (`#00FF00`), pitch terminal black, blood hazard red, warning amber.
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `Cybercore style, glitch art terminal, military cyberware telemetry, Matrix code rainfall, dark UI dashboard, high-tech hacking interface, green phosphor screen glow`.

