### PILLAR 5: Youth Culture, Subversion & Pop

#### 32. Memphis Design
* **Historical Origin:** Founded in Milan by Ettore Sottsass in 1981; radical post-modern architecture/design.
* **Core Identifiers:** Clashing geometric patterns (bacterio pattern squiggles), flat brightly colored laminates, disregard for good taste conventions, playful scale distortions.
* **Palette:** Primary and secondary collisions (Bright lemon, bubblegum magenta, electric teal, high-contrast black-and-white zigzags).
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `Memphis Group design, Ettore Sottsass aesthetic, 1980s post-modern patterns, squiggles and geometric plastic laminates, clashing pop colors, playful unconventional forms`.

#### 33. Pop Art
* **Historical Origin:** Mid-1950s British & American art movement (Andy Warhol, Roy Lichtenstein).
* **Core Identifiers:** Halftone Ben-Day dots, thick heavy black comic outlines, silk-screen color misregistrations, high-contrast commercial iconography, speech bubbles.
* **Palette:** Flat primary CMYK colors (Pure process cyan, process magenta, process yellow, deep black).
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `Roy Lichtenstein Pop Art style, vintage comic book panel, Ben-Day dot pattern, silk-screen misregistration, high-contrast bold ink outlines, dynamic punchy colors`.

#### 34. Graffiti & Street Art
* **Historical Origin:** 1970s New York subway culture, evolving into contemporary urban murals.
* **Core Identifiers:** Drips, fat-cap spray can splatters, expressive wildstyle letterings, stencils on concrete brick walls, torn wheat-paste posters.
* **Palette:** High-visibility neon spray paint, asphalt grey, rust, industrial brick red.
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `Urban street art graffiti, wildstyle lettering, dripping spray paint splatters, weathered concrete wall background, vibrant layered aerosol textures, authentic raw street culture`.

#### 35. Kitsch
* **Historical Origin:** 19th-century commercial mass market aesthetic of cheap, sentimental, or ironic appeal.
* **Core Identifiers:** Deliberate visual excess, fake crystal rhinestones, high-gloss molded plastics, hyper-sentimental pop icons, ironic bad taste.
* **Palette:** Hyper-saturated neon pastels, tacky gold lamé, high-gloss flamingo pink.
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `Ironic kitsch aesthetic, campy visual excess, glossy plastic textures, retro 1960s suburban memorabilia, over-saturated flash photography, intentional bad-taste design`.

#### 36. Pointillism
* **Historical Origin:** Neo-Impressionist painting technique developed by Georges Seurat in 1886.
* **Core Identifiers:** Images formed exclusively through micro-dots of pure color; optical mixing (the eye blends dots at a distance); grain-like visual vibration.
* **Palette:** Broken chromatic tones, impressionist light palettes.
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `Pointillism art style, Georges Seurat technique, composed entirely of micro color dots, stippling optical color blending, textured painterly surface, vibrant visual vibration`.

#### 37. Mixed Media & Collage
* **Historical Origin:** Dadaists (Hannah Höch) and 20th-century editorial graphic design.
* **Core Identifiers:** Ripped magazine paper edges, overlapping halftone photos with rough ink scribbles, textured masking tape, combined digital vector with physical scans.
* **Palette:** Unrestricted; typically combines low-fi vintage newsprint with hyper-vivid modern paint strokes.
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `Mixed media collage art, ripped paper edges, combined vintage photography and hand-painted acrylic textures, visible washi tape, layered dynamic tactile depth`.

#### 38. Scrapbook
* **Historical Origin:** DIY personal journaling and analog photo album culture.
* **Core Identifiers:** Instant camera (Polaroid) white frames, translucent patterned washi tape, craft scissors zig-zag cut edges, handwritten notes, pressed dried leaves.
* **Palette:** Muted nostalgia tones, kraft paper brown, pastel marker accents.
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `Scrapbook journaling aesthetic, physical Polaroid photo frames, washi tape strips, handwritten cursive notes, craft paper collage, warm intimate nostalgic layout`.

#### 39. Conceptual Sketch
* **Historical Origin:** Leonardo da Vinci notebooks, industrial design concept brainstorming.
* **Core Identifiers:** Rapid loose graphite or ink lines, visible construction/perspective guides, crosshatch shading, callout text arrows, textured parchment or blueprint background.
* **Palette:** Graphite pencil grey, sepia ink, blueprint blue, aged cream parchment.
* **Prompt Injection Keywords:** `Industrial design conceptual sketch, loose pencil ideation lines, crosshatched shading, perspective layout lines, technical design notebook page, rough artistic ideation`.

